  <info>
  <link type="guide" xref="reports#other"/>
  <desc>Export what a list shows to a PDF or a spreadsheet.</desc>
    <credit type="author">
      <name>Reuben Rissler</name>
      <email>pygtk.posting@gmail.com</email>
    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Exporting a list</title>

  <p>Many lists have a <gui>Report hub</gui> button or menu item. It opens the
  <gui>Export hub</gui>, which saves the list exactly as it is shown, with the
  same columns, sorting and search.</p>

  <section id="pdf">
  <title>PDF</title>
  <p>On the <gui>Pdf</gui> tab, set the <gui>Border width</gui> and the
  <gui>Font</gui>. The <gui>Layout</gui> is chosen from the list's width:
  portrait when it fits across a letter page, landscape when it does not. A
  warning appears when even landscape is too narrow; you can continue, but
  columns will run off the page, so narrow the window or its columns first.
  Click <gui>Pdf</gui> to see the result, then <gui>Save pdf</gui> or
  <gui>Print</gui>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="xls">
  <title>Spreadsheet</title>
  <p>On the <gui>Xls</gui> tab, click <gui>Xls</gui> and choose where to save
  the file. It opens in your spreadsheet program.</p>
  </section>

</page>
